WEBVTT

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.720
It's not expected in the burning of the Wentworth Castle.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:39.140
Read on about it.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:42.360
Fire at Seymour, you're terrible.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.820
It's just 400 lands lost in accidental burning

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:46.650
in Wentworth Castle.

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:48.150
History, latest X-stree.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:51.210
Millionaire shifting magnet, Cyrus P. Wentworth.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.090
Suspected in ship explosion.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:54.840
Latest X-stree, just now.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:07.350
All my life I see those poor people struggling in the water, drowning.

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:08.990
But it wasn't your fault.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.350
But it was my ship.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:13.400
My company's investigation absolves you completely of all blame.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:17.420
Now then, if you'll be good enough to sign this paper, we can have it with us.

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:21.650
Yes, sir.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.660
I want you to witness my signature.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:25.880
This is Victor Martin, our attorney.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:29.290
Martin, meet Mr. Baldwin of the Mercantile Marine Insurance Company.

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:30.000
How do you do?

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:40.130
Hold on. Here's the check, Mr. Wentworth.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.510
And if I can be of further service, please call on me.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:51.220
Thank you. Good day, gentlemen.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.100
Anything else, sir?

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.080
Do you agree with the changes in the will?

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.420
Oh, yes. Have it with me.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:02.160
Clause 9 is the important one.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.310
Everything goes to your daughter, Cynthia.

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:14.020
It's another problem off my mind.

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:34.650
I hope you'll pardon my mention this, Mr. Wentworth,

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:37.320
but you've been acting very curiously lately.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.140
- Well, now this will. - Well, what?

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:41.880
Kind of man-maker's will?

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:45.090
Of course, but if you're thinking of destroying yourself...

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:47.890
Forget about it. Why should I want to commit suicide?

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:49.870
Well, you're a ship burning and all.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:51.950
I suppose it's been preying on your mind.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.370
But I'm not fool enough to kill myself over it.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:58.450
Well, I'm glad to hear that.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:04.160
- I suppose you'll be going off to your mountain lodge? - Not yet.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:08.840
Why not? You mean that matter of the million and a half in bonds?

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:11.040
Yes, that's on my conscience too.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:13.120
I advised you against accepting that shipment.

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:15.800
I know it. It's the only shady thing I ever did in my life.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:20.020
Then you better go before the maritime commission tomorrow and clear the whole thing up.

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:23.360
- Vicki, are you crazy? - No, it's the only thing to do.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:26.150
But they'll immediately accuse me of sabotaging my own ship.

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:30.000
You'll have to take that chance. I advised you against it when you first asked me

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.580
And now I advise you to go before the commission.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.240
Don't conceal a thing.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:35.800
I'll do it.

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:38.540
I'm sorry I didn't listen to you in the first place.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:39.900
It'll come out all right.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:43.860
I'll see you in the morning.

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:45.360
We'll go before the commission together.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:50.460
Oh, good day, Mr. Flemming.

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:51.460
How are you doing, Mr. Martin?

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:52.670
How's it going?

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:53.670
Fine, thank you.

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:54.680
And yourself?

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:55.530
Never better.

00:04:55.530 --> 00:05:00.000
Could I see Mr. Watworth?

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:01.520
Well, I'll see.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:04.560
Mr. Wentworth, Mr. Fleming Sr. is here.

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:05.420
Certainly, madam.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.040
Yes, sir. You go in, please.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:07.940
Thank you.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:18.890
Hello, Cyrus.

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:23.120
So you've come to gloat over me because one of my ships went down.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:25.320
Oh, you're wrong again, Cyrus.

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:28.270
I came to offer you my sympathy and my help.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:29.800
I don't need your sympathy.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.840
and I can't conceive of any help you could offer.

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:34.920
Now, why can't you see that the consolidation

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:38.780
of our two shipping lines would be a benefit to both of us?

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:40.330
Get this, Fleming.

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:44.590
I'll see my ships all burned before I'll put up with you.

00:05:44.590 --> 00:05:47.640
All right, all right, but what about our kids?

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:49.560
And if you think that you can worm your way

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:52.230
into my business through a family marriage,

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:54.170
you've got another guest coming.

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:55.970
But my boy has no part--

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:57.930
You've never done anything in your life, Fleming,

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:00.000
without an ulterior motive.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.920
All I ask you to do is to keep your office of consolidation away from here

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:08.590
and to keep your boy away from my girl.

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:11.160
- Hello, Mr. Fleming. - Hello, Miss Reed.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:14.590
- Can I see Mr. W? - Well, I think so. Your father's in there.

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:15.760
- Dad? - Yes.

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:27.070
Cyrus, you're a hard-headed, stubborn old fool.

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:28.740
- Oh, Dick. - Hello, Dad.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:35.250
- What are you doing here? - Oh, I came to offer old Cyrus my condolences.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:36.950
I can just imagine how you made out.

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:39.650
And if you're calling on him about what I think you are,

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:41.050
I hope you get a better reception.

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:43.470
Don't worry about me, Dad. I can shout too.

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:46.710
- It's about Cynthia, isn't it? - That's right. She's waiting at the truck for me.

00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:48.790
Regardless of the outcome in there, we're going to get married.

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:50.740
Even if we have to run our way to do it.

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:52.600
Well, at least you have my blessing, son.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:59.100
- Thanks, Dad. - I'm sorry, but he won't see you.

00:06:59.140 --> 00:06:59.880
He won't, eh?

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:07.590
Mr. Wentworth, I have something important to tell you.

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:09.710
Your father's too old to throw out of here, but you're not.

00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:10.310
Get out!

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:11.770
Wait a minute, Mr. Wentworth.

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:13.170
I came here to discuss something--

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:16.060
I'm not interested.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:17.930
All right, I'll put it this way.

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:19.640
I want to marry Cynthia.

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:20.860
No, that's clear.

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:21.580
Isn't it?

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:22.440
Hardly.

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:23.680
What's your objection to me?

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:24.870
Your father.

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:26.910
My father isn't marrying Cynthia.

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:28.300
Neither is his son.

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:30.000
Oh, Mr. Plenty, I'm glad to see you.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:33.840
- Where are you, Matthews? - All right, Miss Reed, here we go.

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:38.770
- I'm sorry to hear about the ship. - Yes, that was a terrible thing.

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:41.670
It's not so much the loss of the ship, it's the loss of lives.

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:45.380
- There's nothing genuine in you. - I wonder who that could be.

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:50.040
My boy, beating the lion in his bed.

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:55.220
Try marrying her against my will and I'll break you in two, sooner or later.

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:57.040
We're not going to let you browbeat us.

00:07:57.460 --> 00:07:59.480
Cynthia and I have gone over this very carefully.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.760
And there's nothing you can do to stop us.

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:03.910
Oh, isn't there?

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:07.430
The conversation was evidently in reference to his daughter.

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:11.490
Get out.

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:12.940
I think I'll wait for the outcome.

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:15.650
I promise you that you can't get away with this sort of thing in this day and age.

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:24.320
Service!

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:42.960
- He's dead. - Call the police?

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:45.460
- No, it just happened. - You gentlemen, stay here.

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:58.560
- Bobby, what do you have? - Same as you.

00:08:58.760 --> 00:08:59.960
Martini, please.

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:01.310
Well, what's up?

00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:04.960
Bobby, I want you to forget you're a newspaper woman for once.

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:06.560
You're going to do a favor for me.

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:08.060
Mm-hmm. What's it this time?

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:09.460
Can you keep a secret?

00:09:09.550 --> 00:09:10.350
A secret?

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:12.050
Now I know it's a story. What is it?

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:13.950
Oh, please, Bobby, we need your help.

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:15.550
We? Yes, Dick and I.

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:16.920
I get it.

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:18.320
So you're going to be married?

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:20.020
Oh, I'll give you a swell break in the paper.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:22.120
Oh, but I don't want you to print anything about it,

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:23.420
at least until it's all over.

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:24.710
That's why I called you.

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:26.210
You're going along with us.

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:28.100
You mean you want me to stand up with you?

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:29.940
Well, always a bridesmaid.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.580
- When do we start? - As soon as I hear from Dick, he's up with Father now, telling him about it.

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:38.980
Even if we can't get Father's consent, we're going to do it anyway.

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:42.750
An elopement! Oh boy, what a spread that'll be!

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:45.580
But my paper gets a story exclusive. It's a deal.

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:47.580
What was the telephone call for you?

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:53.560
Keep your fingers crossed. What's the damage?

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:55.410
Let's see, that will be $4.

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:57.910
What'd she do, buy the place?

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:00.000
No, that's the price. Dollar?

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:02.500
- You're a cocktail. - I'd better take the pearl.

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:04.610
- Keep the change. - Thank you.

00:10:04.610 --> 00:10:09.000
- Oh, Cynthia, why? What's the matter? - It's about father. Something's happened.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:13.220
- I'm calling Mr. Wagner. - I'm calling Mr. Wagner.

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:21.730
- Any trace of the gun, Mike? - Not yet, Cap.

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:23.430
- Did you find anything, Blake? - No.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:26.240
- What's new, Doctor? - Almost instantly. A bullock and a hawk.

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:28.590
- Good job for the corner. - Sure, sure. Open and shut cases.

00:10:28.590 --> 00:10:30.000
This is one time I got the murderer dead to right now.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:33.920
What time did you say that Fleming boy arrived?

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:34.920
Ten past six.

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:35.920
You sure of that?

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:36.920
Absolutely, everybody else had left.

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:38.830
Were you here then?

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:39.830
Yes.

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:40.910
That's sensitive.

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:43.050
If you mean my son, he didn't do it.

00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:44.050
You're the boy's father, aren't you?

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:45.050
Yes.

00:10:45.050 --> 00:10:46.050
Well, we can't take your word for it.

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:47.030
The evidence proves it.

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:48.800
You said you heard loud voices.

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:49.780
Yes.

00:10:49.780 --> 00:10:52.410
Where were you when you heard the shot?

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:53.430
I was out there.

00:10:53.430 --> 00:10:54.430
I was just about to leave.

00:10:54.430 --> 00:10:56.290
And your son thought you were out there?

00:10:56.290 --> 00:10:57.290
No, he thought I had gone.

00:10:57.290 --> 00:10:58.290
Where would he be now?

00:10:58.290 --> 00:10:59.240
Well, I don't know.

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:00.000
You don't seem very well.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.540
You haven't got an appointment to meet him later, have you?

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:03.440
No.

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:05.900
What were you and your son doing here?

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:08.810
Well, I came here to offer my condolences to Mr. Wentworth

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:10.010
over the loss of his ship.

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:11.310
What was the boy doing here?

00:11:11.410 --> 00:11:15.410
He came to ask Mr. Wentworth's permission to marry his daughter.

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:16.310
Oh, that's it.

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:17.710
They had a quarrel and the kid killed him.

00:11:17.810 --> 00:11:18.410
That's all I want to know.

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:19.010
Blake.

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:19.720
Yes, dear.

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:21.730
Did you phone him and have him broadcast that kid's description?

00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:22.330
Yes.

00:11:22.430 --> 00:11:23.590
Says I'm going to have him pick.

00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:25.780
Mr. Fleming, what is it?

00:11:25.880 --> 00:11:26.780
My dear, your father--

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:28.190
What's happened to father?

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:29.590
Please, you must be brave.

00:11:29.690 --> 00:11:30.000
You must be brave.

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:33.200
- Please. - Who are you?

00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:34.600
- She's Cynthia... - Quiet, Logan.

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:37.840
- I'm Cynthia Wentworth. Who are you? - Captain Street of the Homicide Squad.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:40.520
- Homicide Squad? - Yeah, where's Dick for me?

00:11:40.660 --> 00:11:45.640
- Isn't he here? - Please tell me.

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:47.400
- Don't butt in. - All right, Bill.

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:49.880
- Bobby, it's... - Cynthia, darling.

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:56.790
Bobby, it's something terrible, isn't it?

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:25.000
Calling all cars, calling all cars, general broadcast to all stations, be on the watch for Richard Fleming, about 22, five foot eight, light complexion, brown hair, wearing light sport clothes, was last seen in the vicinity of the Wentworth building, he's wanted for murder, don't take any chances, he may be armed and dangerous, that is all.

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:52.340
- You're Richard Fleming, aren't you? - That's right.

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:53.920
You're under arrest for murder.

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:57.150
I want to advise you, anything you say may be used against you.

00:12:57.150 --> 00:12:58.640
- Mike, look for the car over here. - Yeah.

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:08.610
But you must. There's nothing more important than this.

00:13:08.610 --> 00:13:10.640
You've got to do it.

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:15.050
Yes. All right, I'll get it. Bye.

00:13:15.050 --> 00:13:16.960
Hello, Cynthia.

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:18.840
- Oh, Mr... - Matthews.

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:21.680
I was wondering if I could have the passenger list on the boat for my paper.

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:23.180
- Of course. - Thank you.

00:13:23.180 --> 00:13:26.760
Cynthia, I've got some wonderful news for you.

00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:30.000
James Lee Wong, the famous Chinese detective, is going to be special investigation

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:33.060
I've worked with him before, honey, and you've got nothing to worry about.

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:34.060
He's terrific.

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:35.060
Oh, good. Thank you, Bobby.

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:36.060
Here you are.

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:37.060
Oh, thank you.

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:39.080
I'll keep in touch with you, honey.

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:49.100
Casey, Captain Street in.

00:13:49.100 --> 00:13:51.100
Now, wait a minute, Miss Logan.

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:53.370
You're not going to get past me this time.

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:56.580
Captain Street gave strict orders. No one's going in.

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:57.430
Okay, okay.

00:13:57.430 --> 00:13:59.730
I wouldn't think of going in without your permission.

00:14:01.310 --> 00:14:03.890
They picked up the Fleming lad for the murder of old man Wentworth.

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:05.400
The captain's got him in there now.

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:07.600
Oh, boy, this is worth waiting for.

00:14:09.970 --> 00:14:13.230
How many times do I have to tell you I didn't do it?

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:17.850
Everybody knows that you and your father were enemies of Wentworth.

00:14:18.430 --> 00:14:21.650
That you had a quarrel with Wentworth because he wouldn't let you marry his daughter, is that right?

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:23.590
I suppose it is. That still doesn't mean I killed him.

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:26.870
No, but you were the last one with him when he was killed. We can establish that.

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:29.090
Yeah, and why didn't you take the elevator down?

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:30.000
Elevator?

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:32.700
Well, it was only on the second floor.

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:34.230
It was after hours.

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:36.770
I didn't think anything of walking down.

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:38.320
You won't hold water.

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:39.970
Why didn't you leave for the outer office?

00:14:39.990 --> 00:14:42.380
Mr. Wentworth showed me to the hall.

00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:45.770
- Did you know your father was waiting? - No.

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:48.070
Why don't you come clean, kid, and I'll do all I can to help you.

00:14:48.090 --> 00:14:49.950
I don't want your help. I'm innocent, I tell you.

00:14:49.970 --> 00:14:51.030
So you're innocent.

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:53.610
I'm with you there. How are you going to prove your innocence?

00:14:53.630 --> 00:14:55.130
- I don't know. - What did you do with a gun?

00:14:55.150 --> 00:14:56.420
Gun? I didn't have a gun.

00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:59.020
What about this permit issued to you six months ago?

00:14:59.090 --> 00:15:00.000
We had a series of tests.

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:01.960
It's been in my study desk at home.

00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:02.960
I never used it.

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:04.170
Then the gun should still be there.

00:15:04.270 --> 00:15:05.170
That's correct.

00:15:05.270 --> 00:15:07.000
What would you think if I told you I had a man checking

00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:08.300
that the gun is gone?

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:09.000
Gone?

00:15:09.100 --> 00:15:11.000
Look, your own father admits that you were having a violent quarrel

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:13.010
with Wentworth at the time of the shooting.

00:15:13.110 --> 00:15:15.010
Now, if you didn't kill him, you know who did.

00:15:15.110 --> 00:15:17.760
I don't know anything about it.

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:19.760
Did you shoot him in self-defense?

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:21.030
No.

00:15:21.130 --> 00:15:22.980
Kill him in a fit of insanity?

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:26.020
I didn't shoot him, I tell you.

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:26.920
Look, son, don't you see?

00:15:27.770 --> 00:15:30.000
We've established a motive to kill him.

00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:33.580
We've established the fact that you were with Wentworth at the time he was killed.

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:35.120
You haven't got a leg to stand on.

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:36.700
Now, why don't you make a complete confession?

00:15:37.590 --> 00:15:38.490
I didn't do it.

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:40.580
Lock him up, boys.

00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:59.350
All right, all right.

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:02.370
- What do you want? - What's the story?

00:16:02.570 --> 00:16:05.470
- Have you printed anything yet? - No, I'm giving you a break, Bill.

00:16:05.570 --> 00:16:07.130
I'm holding out until I get all the facts.

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:10.230
Well, that's lucky for you, because this is one case I've washed up in a hurry.

00:16:10.330 --> 00:16:11.470
Well, yeah, well, what's the story?

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:13.510
Now, this is the way it ought to be printed. Take it down.

00:16:14.590 --> 00:16:17.380
Two hours after Cyrus P. Wentworth,

00:16:17.480 --> 00:16:20.550
well-known shipping magnate, was found shot to death in his office,

00:16:20.850 --> 00:16:24.540
Captain William Street of the Homicide Squad, acting with lightning-like speed,

00:16:24.700 --> 00:16:27.430
arrested and charged with first-degree murder,

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:30.000
the socially prominent son of Paul Fleming.

00:16:30.570 --> 00:16:33.970
the wrong standing enemy of the Wentworth's interest.

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:35.330
Well, you haven't taken anything down.

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:37.130
Oh, I've got the most important part.

00:16:37.130 --> 00:16:39.250
The lightning-like speed of Captain Street.

00:16:39.250 --> 00:16:40.910
Now, look, this case is closed.

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:43.110
I've got that kid dead to right.

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:47.920
Mr. Wong, I hope I'm not intruding.

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:49.180
Wong, what's brought you here?

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:50.430
I phoned him.

00:16:50.430 --> 00:16:52.190
Are you buttin' into my business again?

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:52.890
Sure.

00:16:52.890 --> 00:16:54.810
I knew you'd arrested the wrong man.

00:16:54.810 --> 00:16:55.650
You always do.

00:16:55.650 --> 00:16:56.490
Now, you listen to me.

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:58.700
I just thought I'd like to check into a few details,

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:00.000
Street, you don't mind, I'm sure.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.100
You're wasting your time, Wong.

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:03.100
Well, time is cheap for those who have it to spend.

00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:03.970
Okay.

00:17:03.970 --> 00:17:06.770
If you can prove to this nosy reporter, then I'm right.

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:10.760
- Did you get the list? - Yes.

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:12.260
What list?

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:14.660
I asked Miss Logan to get me a list of the passengers

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:17.220
who were on the Wentworth Castle when she was burned.

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:19.850
Say, you haven't got a notion that the burning of the Wentworth Castle

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:22.550
had anything to do with that Fleming kid killing Wentworth, have you?

00:17:22.550 --> 00:17:24.830
Well, I've no preconceived notions.

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:27.660
That's more than I can say for you, Bill.

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:29.410
Hmm, interesting.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:32.500
A number of the passengers were Chinese.

00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:34.700
That'll be an investigation, Street.

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:35.700
Why?

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:39.030
Well, you know the burning of the ship was rather suspicious in the first place.

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:43.330
It may be that the relatives of those who were lost have an idea of revenge.

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:45.510
Oh, for the love of mine.

00:17:45.510 --> 00:17:50.270
You mean to tell me that I've got the relatives of 400 drowned people as a speck?

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:52.490
I'm afraid so, Street.

00:17:52.490 --> 00:17:55.190
At any rate, it won't hurt to investigate this list.

00:17:55.190 --> 00:17:56.110
Have at it.

00:17:56.110 --> 00:17:57.690
Is your car here?

00:17:57.690 --> 00:18:00.000
Yes, downstairs. Where can I take it?

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:05.500
- May I borrow Miss Logan? You can have her for a case.

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:07.790
- When we get through with the case,

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:10.920
the Homicide Squad will be the used car squad.

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:15.860
- Yes, Captain, please.

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:18.630
- Have Blake follow Mr. Wong and Miss Logan.

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:21.500
I don't want anything to happen to Mr. Wong.

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:30.000
- Is this the plane?

00:18:31.180 --> 00:18:32.610
No.

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:33.610
You stay here and wait for me.

00:18:33.610 --> 00:18:35.610
I'll be back in a few minutes.

00:18:35.610 --> 00:18:44.850
Logan.

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:14.990
is here on personal business or in his official capacity?

00:19:14.990 --> 00:19:17.350
I am here on behalf of the police.

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:45.970
- You heard of the burning of the Wentworth Castle?

00:19:45.970 --> 00:19:48.090
An unfortunate disaster.

00:19:48.090 --> 00:19:51.540
Do you recognize the names of any of our countrymen on this list?

00:20:01.370 --> 00:20:05.890
One, Kai Ling, the most trusted member of our Tong.

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:09.410
I have no desire to pride in the affairs of the Tong.

00:20:10.450 --> 00:20:12.480
I would like to know the reason of his journey.

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:17.150
He was on a secret mission for the Tong.

00:20:17.890 --> 00:20:19.680
And what was the nature of his mission?

00:20:31.340 --> 00:20:35.720
Kailin was bringing a million and a half in gold bonds from Havana.

00:20:36.450 --> 00:20:36.850
Why?

00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:45.170
Conditions in our country are such that we had to bring the Tong funds to this country for safekeeping.

00:20:46.570 --> 00:20:50.510
It had to be done secretly to avoid international complications.

00:20:50.510 --> 00:20:53.410
So they were being smuggled in aboard the Wentworth Castle.

00:20:55.970 --> 00:20:57.850
Kailin was amongst the survivors.

00:20:58.290 --> 00:20:59.730
So of course you have the bonds.

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:03.840
No, Ki-Ling has disappeared.

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:11.590
You know, of course, that the owner of the Wentworth castle is dead.

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:15.890
No member of this Tongue is guilty of such a deed.

00:21:16.910 --> 00:21:19.910
And no one else had any idea of the existence of the bonds?

00:21:21.230 --> 00:21:25.160
No one else, unless perhaps a rival Tongue.

00:21:25.870 --> 00:21:27.880
- But we can't be sure. - No.

00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:47.660
Thank you.

00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:58.800
Gee, I'm glad you're back.

00:22:06.400 --> 00:22:17.230
I see.

00:22:17.230 --> 00:22:20.570
It's not necessary, the police are off.

00:22:20.570 --> 00:22:27.040
Oh, come on, we're going to the receiving hospital.

00:23:18.680 --> 00:23:30.000
- And this woman. - You might have used a red-hot poker.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:34.780
This is a ridiculous fuss over a simple flesh wound.

00:23:34.780 --> 00:23:37.780
Now, never mind. We're not going to take any chances of infection.

00:23:37.780 --> 00:23:40.730
You've got to have at least one intelligent detective working on the case.

00:23:40.730 --> 00:23:46.810
- How is it, Doc? - Oh, just a flesh wound.

00:23:46.810 --> 00:23:49.630
Now, keep this in the sling for three days.

00:23:49.630 --> 00:23:51.710
- Very well. - All right, Wong. Who shot you?

00:23:51.710 --> 00:23:53.710
- Could have been an accident. - Did I ask you?

00:23:53.710 --> 00:23:56.140
- All right, who did it? - I don't know.

00:23:56.140 --> 00:24:00.000
Now, look, Wong. I had Blake follow you. He saw that guy pull up in that black hole.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.150
and take a shot at you, and you chased him.

00:24:02.150 --> 00:24:03.230
Well, then you know what happened.

00:24:03.230 --> 00:24:03.870
Who was it?

00:24:03.870 --> 00:24:04.490
I don't know.

00:24:04.490 --> 00:24:05.650
The car was wrecked, and when he got there,

00:24:05.650 --> 00:24:08.240
there was nobody in it.

00:24:08.240 --> 00:24:09.960
Must have been a phantom.

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:11.500
Doesn't make any difference who it was.

00:24:11.500 --> 00:24:13.080
Next time you get any wild ideas like this

00:24:13.080 --> 00:24:15.000
and don't tip me off, there's going to be trouble.

00:24:15.000 --> 00:24:16.910
I don't need you on this case, but I might

00:24:16.910 --> 00:24:17.950
need you on a future one.

00:24:17.950 --> 00:24:19.370
So you still think you've solved it, huh?

00:24:19.370 --> 00:24:20.620
Yes, I do.

00:24:20.620 --> 00:24:21.880
Young Fleming didn't.

00:24:21.880 --> 00:24:23.890
And if he didn't, I'll eat my hat.

00:24:23.890 --> 00:24:24.590
I'll see that you do.

00:24:24.590 --> 00:24:26.600
Uh--

00:24:33.290 --> 00:24:37.890
- Thank you, Doctor. - Thank you. Come again.

00:24:38.000 --> 00:24:39.120
I hope last.

00:25:26.810 --> 00:25:28.640
Thomas Reed, I'll see you all in college.

00:25:34.440 --> 00:25:36.870
- Well, Matthews. - Mr. Fleming.

00:25:36.870 --> 00:25:38.960
I'm very happy to know that you've taken over the business.

00:25:38.960 --> 00:25:40.170
Well, thanks.

00:25:40.170 --> 00:25:42.470
Too bad we couldn't have merged before Cyrus died.

00:25:42.470 --> 00:25:44.410
Yes, isn't it a pity?

00:25:44.410 --> 00:25:46.710
We're going to expect you to carry on as usual, Matthews.

00:25:46.710 --> 00:25:47.660
Thanks.

00:25:47.660 --> 00:25:49.690
It's an honor to be associated with you.

00:25:49.690 --> 00:25:52.530
By the way, I'd like to have a digest of the last six months' business.

00:25:52.530 --> 00:25:54.190
Yes, sir. I'll tend to it right away.

00:26:23.000 --> 00:26:24.840
So that's where you put it.

00:26:24.840 --> 00:26:28.100
I knew I saw it on the floor.

00:26:28.100 --> 00:26:30.000
Be rather awkward for you.

00:26:30.030 --> 00:26:33.320
It would be awkward for my son.

00:26:33.320 --> 00:26:38.330
He was in here just before Cyrus committed suicide.

00:26:38.330 --> 00:26:39.330
Before?

00:26:39.330 --> 00:26:40.330
Yes.

00:26:40.330 --> 00:26:44.060
And it was suicide, Matthews.

00:26:44.060 --> 00:26:45.060
It could have been.

00:26:45.060 --> 00:26:48.650
I can swear it was for consideration.

00:26:48.650 --> 00:26:49.650
How much?

00:26:49.650 --> 00:26:56.090
It should be worth a partnership and $25,000.

00:26:56.090 --> 00:26:58.390
Is it a deal?

00:26:58.390 --> 00:26:58.930
Yes.

00:27:03.580 --> 00:27:06.280
- Who's in there? - Mr. Matthews, Mr. Fleming.

00:27:08.060 --> 00:27:14.430
- Is it? - Captain Streep.

00:27:14.440 --> 00:27:20.920
Hello, Mr. Fleming. Special Investigator Wong, Mr. Fleming's father.

00:27:21.020 --> 00:27:22.820
- How do you do? - How do you do, Mr. Wong?

00:27:23.160 --> 00:27:25.160
I've been told that you're going to try to clear my son.

00:27:25.260 --> 00:27:29.730
- Who told you that? - Miss Logan, a friend of my son's fiancée.

00:27:30.090 --> 00:27:31.650
Oh, Wentworth's daughter, huh?

00:27:31.650 --> 00:27:33.730
You know, old man Wentworth didn't sanction this thing.

00:27:33.730 --> 00:27:34.930
Drove the kid to desperation.

00:27:34.930 --> 00:27:36.520
Too bad you had to hear the argument.

00:27:36.520 --> 00:27:41.160
What did Wentworth say that made the kid shoot him?

00:27:41.160 --> 00:27:42.450
How could I be of service?

00:27:42.450 --> 00:27:43.950
Well, first of all, we'd like to know

00:27:43.950 --> 00:27:45.500
what you're doing in this office.

00:27:45.500 --> 00:27:47.140
Well, Miss Wentworth asked me to take over

00:27:47.140 --> 00:27:48.040
her father's business.

00:27:48.040 --> 00:27:49.540
Been waiting a long time for that, haven't you?

00:27:49.540 --> 00:27:51.680
Yes, but I didn't commit murder to get my wish.

00:27:51.680 --> 00:27:54.160
So you had your son do it, isn't that right?

00:27:54.160 --> 00:27:56.200
I was a business rival of Mr. Wentworth,

00:27:56.200 --> 00:27:57.500
but I was not his enemy.

00:27:57.500 --> 00:27:58.960
Of course not.

00:27:58.960 --> 00:28:00.000
I understand that you were

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:03.200
Wong's the first to find the body. Now, just where was it?

00:28:03.200 --> 00:28:08.670
Well, I should say about here.

00:28:08.670 --> 00:28:14.490
Any signs of violence or struggle?

00:28:14.490 --> 00:28:15.600
No.

00:28:15.600 --> 00:28:16.600
You read the police report, Wong?

00:28:16.600 --> 00:28:18.600
Yes, but things can be rearranged, you know.

00:28:18.600 --> 00:28:22.790
By any chance, was there any evidence of that?

00:28:22.790 --> 00:28:25.790
No, I stayed here until the police came and nothing was disturbed.

00:28:25.790 --> 00:28:26.790
I can vouch for that.

00:28:26.790 --> 00:28:29.720
And so neither of you left the room?

00:28:29.720 --> 00:28:30.000
No, sir.

00:28:30.830 --> 00:28:32.170
- Were you out there? - Yes, sir.

00:28:32.170 --> 00:28:33.590
- Hear loud voices? - Yes.

00:28:33.590 --> 00:28:36.470
- To see these two men threaten each other? - I couldn't see them. The door was closed.

00:28:36.470 --> 00:28:39.430
- You know, your boss left a lot of enemies. - Oh, a lot of friends.

00:28:39.430 --> 00:28:41.850
- Would you say that this man and his son were friends? - Yes, I would.

00:28:41.850 --> 00:28:46.590
- What would Wentworth say to that statement? - Well, Mr. Wentworth didn't consider a competitor a friend.

00:28:46.590 --> 00:28:49.510
- Oh, better against him, huh? Particularly his biggest competitor hated him.

00:28:49.510 --> 00:28:52.460
And this man and his son hated Wentworth. - I couldn't say as to that.

00:28:52.460 --> 00:28:55.220
- But you would say that the boy killed him? - No, on the contrary.

00:28:55.220 --> 00:28:58.320
- Who did? - I couldn't tell you.

00:28:58.320 --> 00:29:00.000
- Did you say that he was a suicide?

00:29:00.510 --> 00:29:02.630
Well, he was quite despondent, sir.

00:29:02.920 --> 00:29:04.860
- You've been with this office a long time, haven't you? - Yes, sir.

00:29:05.290 --> 00:29:07.760
- Probably mentioned in the will. - Well, I wouldn't know, sir.

00:29:07.760 --> 00:29:10.100
- Who would? - His attorney, Mr. Martin.

00:29:10.100 --> 00:29:12.780
Suicide clause in that insurance contract would cancel it, wouldn't it?

00:29:12.780 --> 00:29:14.740
- I dare say. - So you took the trouble to hide the gun?

00:29:14.740 --> 00:29:15.620
Oh, no, sir.

00:29:18.320 --> 00:29:22.560
- Here's the list, Mr. Wong. - What list?

00:29:22.680 --> 00:29:24.440
Why do you care? You caught the killer, didn't you?

00:29:24.720 --> 00:29:27.680
I asked the names of all the callers in the office yesterday.

00:29:28.200 --> 00:29:29.640
A man named Lotlow.

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:33.060
- A countryman of mine named Lem Howe.

00:29:33.060 --> 00:29:34.840
- I suppose you saw them.

00:29:34.840 --> 00:29:37.000
- Lem was Mr. Wintle's personal servant.

00:29:37.000 --> 00:29:38.460
Ludlow was discharged chauffeur.

00:29:38.460 --> 00:29:39.660
- Meaning nothing.

00:29:39.660 --> 00:29:41.340
- You say he was discharged?

00:29:41.340 --> 00:29:44.070
- Yes, sir, he came to plead for his job back.

00:29:44.070 --> 00:29:45.050
- What time was that?

00:29:45.050 --> 00:29:47.540
- Early in the day, sir.

00:29:47.540 --> 00:29:50.360
- Shall we go, sweet?

00:29:50.360 --> 00:29:57.490
- Thank you very much, sir.

00:29:57.490 --> 00:29:59.420
- Hey, Wong, they're trying to clear that kid.

00:29:59.420 --> 00:30:00.000
- I'll make you a joke.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:08.090
- I don't need your hat yet! - I found him on the fire escape, Chief.

00:30:08.090 --> 00:30:10.810
- Yeah, who are you? - Chief of police.

00:30:10.810 --> 00:30:14.820
- Why, he's the Wentworth chauffeur. - What were you doing on the fire escape?

00:30:14.820 --> 00:30:18.000
- Locking my car. - Hard to get along with, huh?

00:30:18.000 --> 00:30:21.570
- No, I just don't get chummy with strangers. - That so?

00:30:21.570 --> 00:30:25.240
Ever seen one of those? - Seen a lot of them, haven't you?

00:30:25.240 --> 00:30:29.090
- Don't like cops at all. - You better start talking or I'll lock you up.

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:31.830
- What? - Prowling.

00:30:31.830 --> 00:30:35.840
- Then why were you discharged? - I was a bad, bad boy.

00:30:35.840 --> 00:30:38.200
- I got drunk. - And when was that?

00:30:38.200 --> 00:30:41.850
- A month ago. - Are you looking for trouble?

00:30:41.850 --> 00:30:45.880
No. I'm just trying to find some clue to help the Fleming boy.

00:30:45.880 --> 00:30:50.530
- What's your interest in him? - I'm Miss Cynthia's chauffeur now.

00:30:50.530 --> 00:30:52.800
Aced yourself right back in again, huh?

00:30:52.800 --> 00:30:59.350
- All right, you can go. But don't leave town. - I'll tail him.

00:31:00.320 --> 00:31:01.300
Tough customer, that one.

00:31:01.400 --> 00:31:02.360
I never did like him.

00:31:02.460 --> 00:31:03.620
I wish Cynthia hadn't hired him.

00:31:04.210 --> 00:31:05.230
I'm going to make her fine.

00:31:05.230 --> 00:31:06.670
No, why don't you mind your own business?

00:31:06.670 --> 00:31:08.730
You're always butting into things that don't concern you.

00:31:08.870 --> 00:31:11.510
You sure can stand a lot of work talk, if the talk is big enough.

00:31:11.570 --> 00:31:11.790
Yeah.

00:31:12.180 --> 00:31:13.220
Can I drop you anyplace, Wong?

00:31:13.300 --> 00:31:14.280
Oh, I know where you can drop me.

00:31:14.360 --> 00:31:15.520
Yeah, so do I, on your head.

00:31:21.800 --> 00:31:22.860
Oh, no, Fleming.

00:31:24.320 --> 00:31:25.110
It's gone.

00:31:25.110 --> 00:31:25.410
It's gone.

00:31:39.080 --> 00:31:42.080
- I'm very glad to meet you, Mr. Walling. - Thank you.

00:31:42.600 --> 00:31:46.460
- Cynthia told me you were in the case. - A very curious case, Mr. Martin.

00:31:47.070 --> 00:31:50.310
- Dick is incapable of committing murder. - I agree with you.

00:31:51.080 --> 00:31:54.280
- Is there anyone else that you suspect? - I know of no one to suspect.

00:31:54.280 --> 00:31:55.880
I wish I did for Dick's sake.

00:31:56.580 --> 00:32:00.000
- You were very close to Mr. Webberth, weren't you? - Closer than anyone.

00:32:00.120 --> 00:32:03.560
He gave me my start. I owe him whatever success I had.

00:32:04.070 --> 00:32:06.470
You saw him shortly before his death, didn't you?

00:32:06.720 --> 00:32:07.820
Within the very hour.

00:32:08.330 --> 00:32:10.830
Was anything said at that time that might help us?

00:32:11.890 --> 00:32:12.890
No.

00:32:14.140 --> 00:32:17.040
Matter of his insurance policies on the...

00:32:17.300 --> 00:32:18.600
little dated ship.

00:32:20.260 --> 00:32:22.060
But I believe they're going to be paid.

00:32:22.500 --> 00:32:23.200
They have.

00:32:23.640 --> 00:32:25.140
He's been completely exonerated.

00:32:25.460 --> 00:32:27.560
But he obviously wasn't worrying about that.

00:32:28.690 --> 00:32:30.000
He had been under a strain.

00:32:30.060 --> 00:32:33.960
ever since a disaster in fact I was afraid that he contemplated doing away

00:32:33.960 --> 00:32:40.190
with himself really why because I just made out a new will which he signed then

00:32:40.190 --> 00:32:47.490
seeming anxious to get it over with suicide B but then there's the matter of

00:32:47.490 --> 00:32:52.490
the gun he could hardly dispose of that if he had a bullet in his heart might not

00:32:52.490 --> 00:32:55.370
someone else have taken it to conceal that it was suicide

00:32:55.370 --> 00:33:00.000
I see what you mean the boy for instance perhaps thinking of

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:03.680
I doubt if any man is capable of that much chivalry.

00:33:03.680 --> 00:33:08.340
It's true, isn't it, that the company was in rather low water?

00:33:08.340 --> 00:33:11.220
Even before the Wentworth Castle was burned.

00:33:11.220 --> 00:33:13.690
I thought no one outside knew that.

00:33:13.690 --> 00:33:16.460
Well, I gathered that from the stock market quotations.

00:33:16.460 --> 00:33:18.890
Conditions are not entirely due to the times.

00:33:18.890 --> 00:33:23.830
In fact, large sums of money have been disappearing from the company funds.

00:33:23.830 --> 00:33:28.180
In fact, large sums of money have been disappearing from the company funds.

00:33:28.180 --> 00:33:30.000
Oh.

00:33:30.030 --> 00:33:31.630
besides you and Mr. Wedworth?

00:33:31.630 --> 00:33:32.530
Matthews.

00:33:32.530 --> 00:33:34.350
He had access to the funds?

00:33:34.350 --> 00:33:37.470
Yes, but he's been tireless in his efforts to stop the leak.

00:33:37.470 --> 00:33:40.320
Hmm, I can quite understand that.

00:33:40.320 --> 00:33:45.210
I'm reluctant to believe Matthews was in the same room with Fleming when the shot occurred.

00:33:45.210 --> 00:33:50.680
But Fleming may have turned his back just for the moment that it took to open the door and fire the shot.

00:33:50.680 --> 00:33:52.850
Matthews in the same room?

00:33:52.850 --> 00:33:56.750
If you'll send for your secretary, I'll give you a demonstration.

00:33:56.750 --> 00:33:57.880
Certainly.

00:34:05.630 --> 00:34:08.000
- Yes, sir? - Ms. Wilson, this is Mr. Wong.

00:34:08.040 --> 00:34:09.220
- How do you do? - How do you do?

00:34:09.290 --> 00:34:12.640
If you'll sit down, please.

00:34:12.680 --> 00:34:16.420
If you don't mind, I'm going to try a little experiment with these two coins.

00:34:16.460 --> 00:34:18.190
Now, it's not going to hurt you.

00:34:18.230 --> 00:34:23.030
Now, just close your eyes, and I'll snap these two coins.

00:34:23.070 --> 00:34:26.920
In front of your head, behind your head, and over your head.

00:34:26.960 --> 00:34:29.310
And you tell me where the sound comes from.

00:34:29.520 --> 00:34:30.000
All right.

00:34:30.570 --> 00:34:41.040
- Are your eyes closed? - In the back of my head, in front.

00:34:42.930 --> 00:34:46.610
- Still in front. - Thank you very much.

00:34:48.710 --> 00:34:51.700
- Well, was I right? - Not once.

00:34:52.670 --> 00:34:55.320
- Was there something wrong with me? - Well, hardly.

00:35:05.400 --> 00:35:06.820
That certainly is one for the book.

00:35:08.220 --> 00:35:09.170
I wonder.

00:35:10.010 --> 00:35:12.810
Maybe Dick was in the room with Mr. Wentworth.

00:35:13.050 --> 00:35:14.880
I don't know, but I'll make him tell.

00:35:14.940 --> 00:35:16.900
I don't say a word about the coin trick.

00:35:17.060 --> 00:35:18.520
We may need that in the defense.

00:35:19.410 --> 00:35:20.840
Thank you very much, Mr. Martin.

00:37:53.360 --> 00:37:54.580
God, it's you, Mr. Walton.

00:38:09.660 --> 00:38:11.220
Didn't I see someone at the fire escape?

00:38:11.260 --> 00:38:12.730
You did.

00:38:12.770 --> 00:38:14.730
It was someone who had been opening the safe.

00:38:14.770 --> 00:38:15.940
The safe?

00:38:16.530 --> 00:38:19.950
- Did you recognize him? - It was too dark.

00:38:20.090 --> 00:38:23.690
- Well, we'd better call the police. - No, I don't believe I would if I were you.

00:38:23.730 --> 00:38:25.810
Look, we can't afford to overlook a single clue.

00:38:25.850 --> 00:38:27.650
- Dick's case is getting hopeless. - I know.

00:38:27.670 --> 00:38:29.510
But please don't lose confidence in me.

00:38:30.350 --> 00:38:33.790
I assure you, Miss Wentworth, we are not going to lose your case.

00:38:33.850 --> 00:38:36.930
Thank you, Mr. Wong.

00:38:43.660 --> 00:38:46.810
Funny he didn't make an effort to stop him.

00:38:48.480 --> 00:38:49.960
Look here, Cynthia.

00:38:50.040 --> 00:38:52.880
I don't like this prowling around at night.

00:38:52.960 --> 00:38:55.050
I might have put a bullet through him.

00:38:55.780 --> 00:38:58.490
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:38:58.570 --> 00:39:00.000
After all I've done for you.

00:39:00.280 --> 00:39:02.280
You might at least show a little gratitude.

00:39:04.200 --> 00:39:06.770
Oh, you're not pulling any wool over my eyes, Bill Street.

00:39:06.850 --> 00:39:09.890
You're up to one of your tricks, and I'm going to find out what it is if I'm to camp here all night.

00:39:09.970 --> 00:39:11.630
No, why don't you leave me alone?

00:39:11.710 --> 00:39:14.310
I've told you a thousand times I'm not holding out any news stories on you.

00:39:14.390 --> 00:39:16.840
- Well, then where's Wong? - Oh, I know. I'm not his mother.

00:39:17.900 --> 00:39:20.530
Street, you got Ludlow?

00:39:21.370 --> 00:39:22.510
Yeah. You want him?

00:39:22.590 --> 00:39:24.410
Yes, I'd like to talk to him.

00:39:25.200 --> 00:39:26.590
Blake, bring Ludlow in.

00:39:26.670 --> 00:39:28.090
So you were holding out on me, huh?

00:39:28.170 --> 00:39:30.000
Well, what is this about Ludlow? Come on, give.

00:39:30.120 --> 00:39:32.120
- All right, all right, so my men did pick him up.

00:39:32.120 --> 00:39:34.120
But I haven't got a thing on him. - Oh, don't lie on me.

00:39:34.120 --> 00:39:35.120
Now, wait a minute.

00:39:35.120 --> 00:39:37.240
This female reporter is driving me batty.

00:39:37.240 --> 00:39:40.420
Look, sweetheart, Mr. Wong and I crave secrecy.

00:39:40.420 --> 00:39:42.230
We want to be alone.

00:39:42.230 --> 00:39:44.220
- I don't get the hint. - You don't get the hint?

00:39:44.220 --> 00:39:46.550
Logan, one of these days, I'm going to get my hands

00:39:46.550 --> 00:39:48.550
on that lily-white neck of yours and...

00:39:48.550 --> 00:39:50.660
Curious, Chief.

00:39:50.660 --> 00:39:57.980
So we meet again, Mr. Ludlow.

00:39:57.980 --> 00:40:00.000
The pleasure's all yours.

00:40:01.050 --> 00:40:04.750
Nice of your boys to park their car right underneath my fire escape.

00:40:05.040 --> 00:40:07.240
Do you room and board on that fire escape?

00:40:07.400 --> 00:40:11.360
Oh, now, Miss Logan, why be your usual sweet, nasty self?

00:40:11.810 --> 00:40:15.000
Any time you want a character reference, just come to me.

00:40:15.200 --> 00:40:16.700
Oh, sure, sure.

00:40:17.360 --> 00:40:18.820
You see, we're both the same type.

00:40:19.270 --> 00:40:21.390
You write lies, and I tell them.

00:40:21.570 --> 00:40:23.270
Bill Street, are you going to stand for that?

00:40:23.510 --> 00:40:24.430
Sure.

00:40:25.550 --> 00:40:26.920
Well, Sir Daniel Ludlow?

00:40:26.970 --> 00:40:28.710
Hmm, thanks, Commissioner, I will.

00:40:32.590 --> 00:40:37.330
You know, you'd save us a lot of trouble if you'd just answer one question.

00:40:37.950 --> 00:40:41.260
I'll answer anything you ask, but don't expect the truth.

00:40:41.460 --> 00:40:45.420
Well, I'm quite sure you could tell the truth just once, if you really tried.

00:40:46.050 --> 00:40:48.130
You'd be a fool to believe anything I told you.

00:40:49.010 --> 00:40:51.060
You'll know who killed Wentworth.

00:40:52.680 --> 00:40:55.030
What was on that piece of paper that you burned up?

00:40:56.850 --> 00:40:59.410
Now, who'd ever think that someday I'd be telling the truth?

00:41:00.120 --> 00:41:02.520
What name did you read on that piece of paper?

00:41:03.730 --> 00:41:05.280
I don't know anything about anything.

00:41:05.990 --> 00:41:08.750
You know, I can have you sent up for safe breaking.

00:41:09.350 --> 00:41:10.550
It was open when I got there.

00:41:10.750 --> 00:41:12.740
I'm afraid you'll forget that I was there.

00:41:13.220 --> 00:41:14.790
Oh, then you opened it.

00:41:14.870 --> 00:41:16.870
Oh, why, Mr. Wong.

00:41:17.400 --> 00:41:20.550
I'm quite serious about sending you up.

00:41:22.400 --> 00:41:23.200
And so am I.

00:41:24.030 --> 00:41:24.800
Now, get this.

00:41:25.240 --> 00:41:27.430
I didn't kill the old man, I didn't see it done.

00:41:27.560 --> 00:41:30.000
I ain't making any wild guesses as to who did it.

00:41:30.670 --> 00:41:32.200
If I find out, I'll give you the tip.

00:41:32.200 --> 00:41:34.670
The sooner you quit tailing me and interfering with me,

00:41:34.670 --> 00:41:36.880
the sooner you're going to get that tip, and that's the truth.

00:41:36.880 --> 00:41:38.070
Ha-ha.

00:41:38.070 --> 00:41:40.440
- Lock him up. - No, no, Street.

00:41:40.440 --> 00:41:44.150
I think I'd let him go.

00:41:44.150 --> 00:41:46.260
You don't believe that crook, do you?

00:41:46.260 --> 00:41:48.150
Yes, I do.

00:41:48.150 --> 00:41:50.770
All right, get out of here.

00:41:50.770 --> 00:41:53.170
Thanks for the interview.

00:41:53.170 --> 00:41:58.610
Hope I didn't help you any.

00:42:04.090 --> 00:42:08.830
- I know what he's up to, Streetman. But I think we can anticipate him.

00:42:08.830 --> 00:42:11.230
- Hey, have you got something up your sleeve?

00:42:11.230 --> 00:42:15.370
- Well, there's an answer to every riddle, you know, and I think perhaps this is it.

00:42:15.370 --> 00:42:18.040
- What is that? - Ashes.

00:42:18.040 --> 00:42:21.040
- Oh, look, we're trying to solve a murder and you're carrying ashes around.

00:42:21.040 --> 00:42:23.790
- Is that going to tell us who killed Wentworth?

00:42:23.790 --> 00:42:26.800
- No, but it may be a clue as to the reason of the killing.

00:42:26.800 --> 00:42:30.000
And once we know that, we are very close to knowing the idea.

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:31.570
the identity of the killer.

00:42:32.240 --> 00:42:34.340
We'll need some infrared film, Street.

00:42:34.460 --> 00:42:36.270
You better use a photographic lab.

00:42:36.420 --> 00:42:37.000
Right.

00:42:37.080 --> 00:42:39.000
Well, what's infrared film for?

00:42:39.760 --> 00:42:43.140
Photograph the ashes and I hope to bring out the writing on them.

00:42:43.380 --> 00:42:45.390
Oh, but who?

00:42:45.710 --> 00:42:46.830
Look, dummy.

00:42:46.960 --> 00:42:51.570
Infrared film is sensitive to wavelengths of light beyond the human eye.

00:43:49.900 --> 00:43:51.960
- Fascinating. - Who, me?

00:43:52.370 --> 00:43:56.330
- No, the other negative. - And you look good too, in the dark.

00:44:23.870 --> 00:44:27.330
- Find anything more? - Not yet. It's rather faint.

00:44:39.340 --> 00:44:40.540
There goes the clue.

00:44:41.220 --> 00:44:44.900
Well, I found one name, Kai Ling.

00:44:45.020 --> 00:44:46.100
He was one of the passengers.

00:44:46.220 --> 00:44:47.980
Yeah, yeah, we heard that before.

00:44:48.600 --> 00:44:49.720
Kai Ling.

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:04.440
Why? We've got all we need. We have Cai Ling's name.

00:45:05.390 --> 00:45:07.240
James Lee Wong speaking.

00:45:08.810 --> 00:45:10.920
Have you a record of Cai Ling?

00:45:11.750 --> 00:45:13.690
I'd like his address, please.

00:45:14.940 --> 00:45:17.320
19 Queen Street on the waterfront.

00:45:17.940 --> 00:45:19.650
Thank you.

00:45:19.890 --> 00:45:20.720
Do you want him?

00:45:20.910 --> 00:45:22.630
Yes, I'll pick him up myself.

00:45:23.310 --> 00:45:26.600
And don't phone your editor. I'll tip you off when.

00:45:32.490 --> 00:45:36.410
Now, you make another negative imprint of that and don't let anybody see it but me.

00:45:36.410 --> 00:45:37.520
All right, Mr. Walls.

00:46:06.140 --> 00:46:07.520
You'd better turn your lights off.

00:47:04.120 --> 00:47:07.360
- No one's home, Bill. Let's go. - Why don't you see if some windows are open?

00:47:07.360 --> 00:47:09.820
- Who, me? - Yeah.

00:47:09.820 --> 00:47:12.120
I thought you newspaper gals were brave.

00:47:12.120 --> 00:47:14.960
Yeah, and I thought a man as big as you could break in a front door.

00:47:14.960 --> 00:47:25.830
Ah, I'm brave.

00:47:30.700 --> 00:47:32.660
You stay out of my way and quit following me.

00:47:32.660 --> 00:47:53.110
It's me, it's me.

00:48:22.590 --> 00:48:25.830
- Logan. - Bobby.

00:48:37.070 --> 00:48:38.870
- What's the matter? - In there.

00:48:48.860 --> 00:48:57.910
I can't find a light. This guy's cold.

00:49:00.640 --> 00:49:04.070
- That doesn't work. - Light that candle.

00:49:57.230 --> 00:49:58.810
- Do you think it's Kai Ling?

00:49:58.810 --> 00:50:00.000
- Just a minute.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:03.500
- How do I know who he is? - Well, it's a story anyway.

00:50:03.500 --> 00:50:06.300
- Bobby Logan discovered... - Bobby Logan discovered nothing.

00:50:06.300 --> 00:50:08.870
I'll tell you when to print the story.

00:50:46.700 --> 00:50:47.920
Did you let go of me?

00:51:04.320 --> 00:51:12.360
- What did you send me for if you were coming down here? - I'm not in the street. I'm coming up.

00:51:12.360 --> 00:51:25.580
- Very funny. - Very funny.

00:51:25.580 --> 00:51:28.770
I don't know. I'm coming up.

00:51:34.090 --> 00:51:36.090
I gave Miss Logan rather a shock.

00:51:36.090 --> 00:51:37.360
Thanks.

00:51:37.360 --> 00:51:40.360
You're sure this is the right address that they gave us over the telephone?

00:51:40.360 --> 00:51:41.730
Yes.

00:51:41.730 --> 00:51:43.640
Ah.

00:51:43.640 --> 00:51:46.690
Tyling was a passenger on the Wentworth Castle.

00:51:46.690 --> 00:51:49.480
He lives here on the waterfront.

00:51:49.480 --> 00:51:51.480
I think he's in the smuggling business.

00:51:51.480 --> 00:51:53.480
You mean he was in the smuggling business?

00:51:53.480 --> 00:51:54.330
Come on.

00:52:11.160 --> 00:52:25.860
What about A?

00:52:25.860 --> 00:52:27.680
Very old dynasty.

00:52:27.680 --> 00:52:28.710
Who, this guy?

00:52:33.480 --> 00:52:37.080
It's a strange thing that the rest of the house should be empty

00:52:37.280 --> 00:52:39.790
while this room is elaborately furnished.

00:52:40.970 --> 00:52:43.370
He must have been a person of considerable importance.

00:52:43.570 --> 00:52:46.170
Yes, and he had something important or they wouldn't have murdered him.

00:52:50.700 --> 00:52:59.600
Turn his head so that we can see his face.

00:53:03.000 --> 00:53:06.170
I've been dead for some days.

00:53:06.170 --> 00:53:08.610
You know, this is the right address that they gave us.

00:53:08.610 --> 00:53:11.440
This must be Kai Ling.

00:53:11.440 --> 00:53:14.440
Bell Street, what do you mean, leaving me downstairs unconscious?

00:53:14.440 --> 00:53:17.140
That's nothing new.

00:53:17.140 --> 00:53:19.640
Oh, that's Lim. How? The missing Wentworth sermon.

00:53:19.640 --> 00:53:20.640
How do you know?

00:53:20.640 --> 00:53:23.170
Oh, I've seen him lots of times.

00:53:23.170 --> 00:53:25.670
He killed Wentworth and then committed suicide.

00:53:25.670 --> 00:53:28.980
Sure, stabbed himself in the back. You're still unconscious.

00:53:28.980 --> 00:53:30.000
Treat.

00:53:31.180 --> 00:53:35.580
Do you suppose that Kai Ling and Lem Hao are one and the same person?

00:53:40.830 --> 00:53:43.300
Where did you get that stuff?

00:53:43.300 --> 00:53:45.400
I phoned Miss Wentworth and she sent it.

00:53:46.290 --> 00:53:47.690
You sure you didn't phone her?

00:53:47.690 --> 00:53:49.190
Bill Street, of course I didn't.

00:53:49.190 --> 00:53:50.590
You know, you made me a promise.

00:53:50.590 --> 00:53:51.490
Well, I kept it.

00:53:51.490 --> 00:53:52.690
This story breaks out.

00:53:52.690 --> 00:53:55.190
I'm sorry, Street, but I'm afraid it's broken already.

00:53:55.620 --> 00:53:56.660
How could it?

00:53:56.750 --> 00:53:59.850
Well, you see, Miss Logan was with me when I telephoned Miss Wentworth.

00:54:00.280 --> 00:54:02.680
And she said it's too bad this story can't be published.

00:54:02.780 --> 00:54:05.100
It might influence public opinion in favor of Dick.

00:54:05.560 --> 00:54:07.280
And I'm afraid Miss Wentworth heard it.

00:54:07.680 --> 00:54:08.900
So you shouted, huh?

00:54:09.000 --> 00:54:10.040
Well, I didn't talk direct.

00:54:10.140 --> 00:54:12.890
Uh, Street?

00:54:13.760 --> 00:54:16.130
Same handwriting.

00:54:16.770 --> 00:54:18.890
Lem Howe and Kai Ling are one of the same person.

00:54:18.990 --> 00:54:20.070
We have something here.

00:54:20.510 --> 00:54:21.750
Yeah, a Chinese puzzle.

00:54:21.850 --> 00:54:22.990
Then Lem Howe did do it.

00:54:23.240 --> 00:54:25.880
Cynthia said that he and her father had an argument a short time ago.

00:54:25.940 --> 00:54:26.380
Quiet.

00:54:27.270 --> 00:54:28.210
Long, if this Lem Howe...

00:54:28.210 --> 00:54:30.000
I've got as much right as this discussion.

00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:31.000
Will you be quiet?

00:54:31.000 --> 00:54:31.950
Well, I found the corpse, didn't I?

00:54:31.950 --> 00:54:32.950
All right, all right.

00:54:32.950 --> 00:54:33.950
Finish what you're going to say, will you?

00:54:33.950 --> 00:54:34.950
Well, I did finish.

00:54:34.950 --> 00:54:35.950
It's simple.

00:54:35.950 --> 00:54:36.950
Sure you're simple.

00:54:36.950 --> 00:54:38.950
He shot Wentworth and then killed himself.

00:54:38.950 --> 00:54:40.970
Just stabbed himself in the back, huh?

00:54:40.970 --> 00:54:43.080
Well, Wong in Oriental Wood, wouldn't he?

00:54:43.080 --> 00:54:46.080
You know, commit hairy-hairy or whatever you call it.

00:54:46.080 --> 00:54:48.670
Hairy-hairy.

00:54:48.670 --> 00:54:55.040
Hello, straight speaking.

00:54:55.040 --> 00:54:58.390
What?

00:54:58.390 --> 00:54:59.640
What?

00:55:02.270 --> 00:55:07.110
Yeah, okay. Suicide, huh? Come here, Wong.

00:55:07.210 --> 00:55:09.890
This is a pip. I had an autopsy performed.

00:55:10.040 --> 00:55:11.940
They found a bullet wound underneath the dagger.

00:55:12.060 --> 00:55:14.080
They traced the bullet through the body into the hip.

00:55:14.100 --> 00:55:16.750
And that bullet came from the same gun that killed Wentworth.

00:55:19.210 --> 00:55:19.840
Yeah?

00:55:20.120 --> 00:55:22.910
Wentworth and Mr. Martin. Shall I send them in?

00:55:23.010 --> 00:55:25.460
Wait a minute. Oh, that's swell. That's fine.

00:55:25.560 --> 00:55:27.360
Now you got that Wentworth gal on my neck.

00:55:28.700 --> 00:55:29.890
Now get this, Bobby.

00:55:30.480 --> 00:55:31.880
This is strictly between us.

00:55:32.040 --> 00:55:35.040
If a word of this gets out, something's going to happen and I'm not fooling.

00:55:35.170 --> 00:55:35.970
Okay, Bill.

00:55:37.380 --> 00:55:39.580
I'm not going to try and pin this on the Fleming kid.

00:55:39.790 --> 00:55:42.600
It's a little far-fetched that he'd commit a couple of murders the same day.

00:55:43.230 --> 00:55:45.230
But I am going to check on his whereabouts that morning.

00:55:45.520 --> 00:55:46.720
If only to protect him.

00:55:47.290 --> 00:55:48.190
Now listen, Dizzy.

00:55:48.600 --> 00:55:50.000
I'm going to leave you alone with him.

00:55:50.030 --> 00:55:52.330
I want you to get that information and I'm not fooling.

00:55:52.430 --> 00:55:53.230
You understand?

00:55:53.640 --> 00:55:54.200
Yes.

00:56:00.570 --> 00:56:02.500
Casey, have Fleming brought up. Come in.

00:56:03.270 --> 00:56:05.320
Bobby, how are you?

00:56:06.000 --> 00:56:08.880
- Have you found anything? - A lot.

00:56:09.080 --> 00:56:11.480
Well, that is good news. Whatever it is, don't delay.

00:56:11.590 --> 00:56:13.290
Anything to postpone the hearing.

00:56:13.410 --> 00:56:16.970
I've done my best, but I'm stymied by a mountain of circumstantial evidence.

00:56:17.170 --> 00:56:18.570
I can realize that.

00:56:18.740 --> 00:56:22.430
I'm afraid your servant, Lem Howe, is dead, Miss Wentworth.

00:56:22.630 --> 00:56:25.630
- Lem? Dead? - It may have a bearing on the case.

00:56:25.800 --> 00:56:28.740
He was found in an old house in the Chinese Quarter.

00:56:28.930 --> 00:56:29.960
He'd been murdered.

00:56:30.510 --> 00:56:32.140
Murdered?

00:56:32.140 --> 00:56:35.380
It must be someone who is determined to destroy the entire household.

00:56:35.380 --> 00:56:39.410
In heaven's name, Captain, don't let this girl go around without a bodyguard.

00:56:39.410 --> 00:56:41.310
- You're right. I'll arrange for one. - But no one...

00:56:41.310 --> 00:56:43.310
And fire that chauffeur. It gives me the chill.

00:56:43.310 --> 00:56:46.420
I haven't seen him for 24 hours. I guess he's fired himself.

00:56:46.420 --> 00:56:50.720
- Why did you take him back? - He promised to stay sober and to help Dick.

00:56:50.720 --> 00:56:52.900
And two, he said I could use a bodyguard.

00:56:52.900 --> 00:56:55.600
Great guns. I'd rather have a rattlesnake following me.

00:56:55.600 --> 00:56:59.320
- Dick. - Cynthia.

00:57:00.920 --> 00:57:03.080
I'm going to leave you alone for a quarter of an hour.

00:57:03.160 --> 00:57:04.280
No one will bother you.

00:57:04.290 --> 00:57:05.700
Come on, woman.

00:57:06.760 --> 00:57:11.560
- Are you all right? - Of course I am, my darling.

00:57:11.560 --> 00:57:15.600
Dick, you can come clean on something now, I've got to know.

00:57:15.680 --> 00:57:17.600
It may be a chance of proving your innocence.

00:57:17.940 --> 00:57:21.250
If you were in that office when the shot was fired, you've got to say so.

00:57:31.150 --> 00:57:33.100
If I was, I would have seen the killer.

00:57:33.100 --> 00:57:35.050
No, you might only have heard the shot.

00:57:35.050 --> 00:57:37.050
Well, I certainly would have known where it came from.

00:57:37.050 --> 00:57:38.940
Not necessarily, as Wong can demonstrate.

00:57:38.940 --> 00:57:40.960
I know, I've seen him do it.

00:57:40.960 --> 00:57:42.390
You were there, weren't you?

00:57:42.390 --> 00:57:48.410
Yes, I was stunned.

00:57:48.410 --> 00:57:51.810
The outer hall door had been opened by Mr. Wentworth when he asked me to leave.

00:57:51.810 --> 00:57:57.640
When he fell at my feet, I turned into the hall and ran to intercept whoever had done it.

00:57:57.640 --> 00:58:00.000
And I returned unsuccessfully.

00:58:00.920 --> 00:58:04.040
I saw people running into the outer office, and I knew at once I'd be accused.

00:58:04.560 --> 00:58:05.700
So I'd be it for home.

00:58:07.160 --> 00:58:10.120
If I tell that to the court, the walls and all would fall down on top of me.

00:58:10.660 --> 00:58:13.610
If you'd only told me this before, we might have had something to go on.

00:58:13.870 --> 00:58:17.350
The open door, fingerprints, concentrate.

00:58:17.700 --> 00:58:19.470
Can't you remember having seen someone?

00:58:19.780 --> 00:58:20.980
But I didn't see anybody.

00:58:21.180 --> 00:58:23.720
Dick, where were you before you went to the Wentworth office?

00:58:23.960 --> 00:58:27.360
That morning, I took Cynthia to get a good view of the burnt ship.

00:58:27.560 --> 00:58:29.760
Lem was there. He'd lost a cousin to somebody.

00:58:30.000 --> 00:58:33.080
Then I drove Cynthia to the truck, and I took Lemme to Chinatown.

00:58:33.080 --> 00:58:35.480
Chinatown? Oh, Dick!

00:58:35.480 --> 00:58:36.330
Well, so what?

00:58:36.330 --> 00:58:40.090
You took Lemme to Chinatown, and no one's seen him alive since.

00:58:40.090 --> 00:58:56.670
Oh, shh! Big lug. It's a frame-up.

00:58:56.670 --> 00:58:58.170
Dick, you're going to escape.

00:58:58.170 --> 00:59:00.000
Bobby, go out that door.

00:59:00.120 --> 00:59:01.860
My car's in the alley and the keys are in it.

00:59:01.860 --> 00:59:03.280
Take Cynthia with you and go on home.

00:59:03.280 --> 00:59:04.740
No one will ever look for you there.

00:59:04.740 --> 00:59:06.840
Stop! Do you want him to hang himself completely?

00:59:06.840 --> 00:59:08.240
He'll give us more time.

00:59:08.240 --> 00:59:10.060
Dick, if you're going through with this mad impulse,

00:59:10.060 --> 00:59:11.150
wait till I'm out.

00:59:11.150 --> 00:59:13.050
I'd be disbarred if I were a witness to it.

00:59:13.050 --> 00:59:15.800
Well, then go on.

00:59:15.800 --> 00:59:17.670
All right.

00:59:17.670 --> 00:59:18.810
Go on, hurry up.

00:59:18.810 --> 00:59:22.010
I'll meet you later, go on.

00:59:22.010 --> 00:59:24.480
Nice work, baby, nice work.

00:59:24.480 --> 00:59:26.580
I got just what I wanted, just what I wanted.

00:59:26.580 --> 00:59:30.000
I wonder what happened to that mic.

00:59:31.400 --> 00:59:33.360
Oh, I guess somebody tripped over it.

00:59:33.980 --> 00:59:35.760
Where'd they go?

00:59:35.880 --> 00:59:37.200
Well, they finished and left.

00:59:37.520 --> 00:59:39.210
That's so?

00:59:39.590 --> 00:59:41.130
You ought to have your head examined.

00:59:41.590 --> 00:59:43.120
That's been open all the time.

00:59:43.220 --> 00:59:44.420
You heard everything?

00:59:44.520 --> 00:59:46.220
Sure, and we're going to join him for tea later,

00:59:46.320 --> 00:59:47.620
as soon as he digs up that gun.

00:59:47.720 --> 00:59:49.020
Why, you big baboon!

00:59:49.120 --> 00:59:50.620
Oh, I've got the Fleming place covered.

00:59:50.720 --> 00:59:52.790
Anybody can get in, but nobody can get out.

00:59:52.810 --> 00:59:53.310
What?

00:59:53.410 --> 00:59:54.800
Oh, no, you don't.

00:59:54.950 --> 00:59:57.170
Nothing but a divorce can separate us now.

00:59:57.270 --> 00:59:58.780
We'd have to get married to get a divorce,

00:59:58.880 --> 00:59:59.680
and I wouldn't marry you.

00:59:59.780 --> 01:00:00.000
If I were the last one.

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:02.650
He's the best man on earth, I know. Sit down.

01:00:16.990 --> 01:00:20.390
- Is that on bail? - No, he's escaped.

01:00:38.600 --> 01:00:40.110
I've escaped.

01:00:40.110 --> 01:00:41.310
Dick, you've convicted yourself.

01:00:41.310 --> 01:00:42.510
I'm convicted as it is.

01:00:42.510 --> 01:00:44.410
The police, Martin, everyone thinks I haven't a chance.

01:00:44.410 --> 01:00:45.410
Why shouldn't I run away?

01:00:45.410 --> 01:00:46.410
But don't you see?

01:00:46.410 --> 01:00:47.410
You're confessing your guilt.

01:00:47.410 --> 01:00:48.410
What's the difference?

01:00:48.410 --> 01:00:49.410
Everybody thinks I'm guilty.

01:00:49.410 --> 01:00:50.740
You've got to get me out of here.

01:00:50.740 --> 01:00:51.740
You've got to get a plane for me.

01:00:51.740 --> 01:00:52.660
No, go back.

01:00:52.660 --> 01:00:55.660
I'm not a quitter, but I haven't anything to fight with.

01:00:55.660 --> 01:00:57.660
I can't fight locked in a stinking jail.

01:00:57.660 --> 01:00:58.870
Go back, son.

01:00:58.870 --> 01:01:00.000
You won't help.

01:01:03.520 --> 01:01:06.470
- You think I did it too, don't you, Dad? - Well, don't say that to me.

01:01:06.470 --> 01:01:11.000
Dick, please. It was Bobby's idea to give Wong more time.

01:01:11.000 --> 01:01:16.370
You have nothing to fear, son. I can clear you.

01:01:16.370 --> 01:01:17.350
How?

01:01:17.350 --> 01:01:23.100
If it looks like a conviction, I'll tell the court who did it and how it was done.

01:01:23.100 --> 01:01:24.450
You know?

01:01:46.000 --> 01:01:47.640
- Who is it? - Matthew.

01:02:11.230 --> 01:02:14.510
I thought he was just as far away when the trial opened.

01:02:14.510 --> 01:02:16.520
Have you the balance?

01:02:16.520 --> 01:02:17.760
No.

01:02:17.760 --> 01:02:19.840
I phoned you long before the banks closed.

01:02:19.840 --> 01:02:22.360
No more money for you, Matthews.

01:02:22.360 --> 01:02:25.250
Are you forgetting that what you did means your son's finished?

01:02:25.250 --> 01:02:27.390
They'll hang him.

01:02:27.390 --> 01:02:29.340
I'm not paying you anymore.

01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:31.940
Shall I call the police?

01:02:31.940 --> 01:02:36.990
I'll save you the trouble.

01:02:36.990 --> 01:02:42.710
See, I wouldn't do that if I were you.

01:02:42.710 --> 01:02:44.790
You're making a mistake.

01:02:44.790 --> 01:02:46.930
Could I have the detective bureau, please?

01:02:46.930 --> 01:02:47.970
Detective bureau?

01:02:47.970 --> 01:02:50.840
You're making a terrible mistake, Dr. Fleming.

01:02:50.840 --> 01:02:52.370
I'd like to speak to Captain Street.

01:03:01.950 --> 01:03:05.410
- Hello? - Captain Street, Mrs. Fleming.

01:03:05.410 --> 01:03:12.280
- Yes, Mr. Fleming. - Captain, my son did not kill Cyrus Wentworth.

01:03:12.280 --> 01:03:16.640
If you'll come to my house, I'll tell you who did it.

01:03:16.640 --> 01:03:25.590
- Fleming, shut up! - Shut up!

01:03:25.590 --> 01:03:27.520
- Where's the car? - In the alley.

01:03:56.780 --> 01:04:00.000
-Shut, Fleming. -Anybody leave?

01:04:00.380 --> 01:04:10.500
- How is he? - He's a bad wound, but he's not fatal.

01:04:12.590 --> 01:04:18.780
Fleming, this is Captain Street. What were you trying to tell me on the phone?

01:04:20.160 --> 01:04:23.310
- I killed Sarris, went away. - Ted, you don't know what you're saying.

01:04:23.530 --> 01:04:27.140
- All right, I'm listening. - Matthew saw me do it.

01:04:27.300 --> 01:04:30.000
I've had to pay him for his service.

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:32.290
Oh, so he shot you?

01:04:32.290 --> 01:04:35.650
Just relax. The doc will be here in a minute.

01:04:35.650 --> 01:04:37.650
Des, you're not telling the truth. He's only trying to protect me.

01:04:37.650 --> 01:04:39.650
Take it easy, kid. Just hold everything.

01:04:39.650 --> 01:04:41.650
I'll get to the bottom of this.

01:04:41.650 --> 01:04:49.160
Well, you heard what he said?

01:04:49.160 --> 01:04:50.160
Yes.

01:04:50.160 --> 01:04:51.180
Did you see him kill Wentworth?

01:04:51.180 --> 01:04:52.180
No.

01:04:52.180 --> 01:04:53.030
What do you mean, no?

01:04:53.030 --> 01:04:54.030
Well, he might have. I don't know.

01:04:54.030 --> 01:04:55.920
But I did see him hide the gun.

01:04:55.920 --> 01:04:57.780
So you used that to blackmail him, huh?

01:04:57.780 --> 01:04:58.900
That's all I want to know.

01:05:02.720 --> 01:05:05.960
- Well, that eliminates the Fleming, kid. - It depends on the father.

01:05:06.810 --> 01:05:16.010
I've never heard your very fine gesture, Mr. Fleming.

01:05:16.290 --> 01:05:17.890
Quite unnecessary.

01:05:21.320 --> 01:05:24.740
- The pleasure is... - Well, the pleasure is still mine.

01:05:24.830 --> 01:05:26.970
You got past me in the garden, didn't you?

01:05:27.080 --> 01:05:30.000
But fortunately for Mr. Fleming, your aim was not as good as...

01:05:30.000 --> 01:05:32.120
that's when you killed Kai Ling and Mr. Wentworth.

01:05:32.480 --> 01:05:34.710
- I killed Wentworth? - Of course you did.

01:05:35.090 --> 01:05:38.930
From across the hall through the open door and then you threw the gun into the room.

01:05:39.300 --> 01:05:41.100
And you hoped to implicate young Fleming.

01:05:41.300 --> 01:05:43.250
No, you're making that up out of your head.

01:05:43.520 --> 01:05:44.240
Am I?

01:05:45.080 --> 01:05:48.280
And I suppose I'm imagining that you had to destroy the agreement

01:05:48.360 --> 01:05:49.960
between Kai Ling and Wentworth.

01:05:50.010 --> 01:05:53.590
- What agreement? - That piece of paper that you were burning in the office that night.

01:05:53.830 --> 01:05:55.900
- Your name was on it. - My name wasn't on it.

01:05:56.100 --> 01:05:58.390
- Your name was on it as a witness, wasn't it? - It was not.

01:05:58.770 --> 01:05:59.600
That's right.

01:06:00.320 --> 01:06:01.480
Wentworth showed me the paper.

01:06:02.000 --> 01:06:03.060
It was his signature.

01:06:03.830 --> 01:06:05.570
Why, you double-crawling...

01:06:05.570 --> 01:06:06.450
There's a man, Street.

01:06:07.160 --> 01:06:07.830
Take a mic.

01:06:10.000 --> 01:06:12.530
So you were partners.

01:06:13.300 --> 01:06:18.480
Well, I really am surprised that a professional like you would team up with an amateur like this.

01:06:18.930 --> 01:06:19.870
Here's the gun, Street.

01:06:20.010 --> 01:06:20.930
I traced it to him.

01:06:21.850 --> 01:06:25.990
And here's the reproduction of the burned agreement with Martin's signature on it.

01:06:34.190 --> 01:06:36.590
Sorry, I had to hold that out on you, but...

01:06:36.810 --> 01:06:38.410
- There's only one thing I regret. - I know.

01:06:38.510 --> 01:06:41.630
That you didn't kill me that night in Chinatown when you shot at me.

01:06:41.910 --> 01:06:49.380
- Take them out, boys. - Well, Street...

01:06:50.260 --> 01:06:52.720
- We've done it again. - Yeah, sure.

01:06:52.800 --> 01:06:56.100
Why, the first day in the office, I had this whole thing doped out.

01:06:56.290 --> 01:06:56.920
Yeah.

01:07:05.760 --> 01:07:10.120
What am I doing?
